<Window x:Class="VaccineAssist.Desktop.Views.MacroCodesWindow"
        xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
        xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
        xmlns:wv2="clr-namespace:Microsoft.Web.WebView2.Wpf;assembly=Microsoft.Web.WebView2.Wpf"
        Title="Macro codes"
        Width="1375" Height="1025"
        WindowStyle="ToolWindow"
        Topmost="True"
        ShowInTaskbar="False"
        ResizeMode="NoResize"
        WindowStartupLocation="CenterScreen"
        PreviewKeyDown="MacroCodesWindow_OnPreviewKeyDown">
    <!--
        Will, 2026-09-13 (verbatim): "Make a macro code popup ... this
        screen we built when someone pushes Ctrl+8. When they click on the
        one they want, it copies the macro code and closes the page so
        they can go resume data entry themselves."

        Hosts the cloud app's /macro-codes?embed=1 page (built alongside
        this — see the cloud side's macro-codes route) in-process via
        WebView2 rather than the user's default browser, so it can stay a
        borderless, Topmost, non-taskbar popup exactly like
        DataEntryPopupWindow — same "quick popup while working the Rx
        profile" workflow, just for looking up a macro code instead of
        entering a dose. WindowStartupLocation="CenterScreen" and the
        Topmost/ShowInTaskbar/ResizeMode combination match
        DataEntryPopupWindow.xaml's existing convention.

        2026-09-13 (Will, verbatim, after testing the popup): "It works.
        The page needs to be compact ... so that it will fit all on one
        popup and not require scrolling." The cloud page's embed mode
        (?embed=1, app/macro-codes/page.tsx) was rebuilt to fit its
        content within an estimated ~534px inside a 980x760 window with
        no scrolling — see that file's "EMBED COMPACT" comment for the
        height budget. Bumped from 980x760 to 1100x820 here anyway, purely
        for extra headroom around that estimate; the cloud CSS still
        targets 980x760, so this leaves margin rather than requiring it.

        2026-09-25 round 2 (Will, verbatim): "Make the maro code popup be
        a litle bigger." Bumped again, ~25%, from 1100x820 to 1375x1025 —
        see MacroCodesWindow.xaml.cs's constructor for the
        SystemParameters.WorkArea clamp that keeps this from exceeding the
        visible desktop on a smaller monitor while staying centered. Same
        popup class/size for both the Ctrl+Keypad 8 flow and the age-macro
        flow (they share this window).

        The page copies the code itself and posts
        window.chrome.webview.postMessage({ type: "vaccine-assist:macro-copied",
        code, label, product }) back to this host; Escape (here, via
        PreviewKeyDown) or the page's own
        { type: "vaccine-assist:macro-cancel" } message both just close
        the popup with no clipboard action. See MacroCodesWindow.xaml.cs.
    -->
    <Grid>
        <wv2:WebView2 x:Name="WebView"/>

        <!-- Shown instead of the WebView2 control if CoreWebView2
             initialization throws (e.g. the WebView2 Runtime isn't
             installed on this workstation) — see
             MacroCodesWindow_OnLoaded's catch clause. Never lets a missing
             runtime crash the app; just explains what to do. -->
        <StackPanel x:Name="FailurePanel" Visibility="Collapsed"
                    VerticalAlignment="Center" HorizontalAlignment="Center" Margin="32">
            <TextBlock Text="Couldn't load the macro codes screen." FontWeight="Bold" FontSize="14"
                       TextWrapping="Wrap" HorizontalAlignment="Center"/>
            <TextBlock Margin="0,10,0,0" TextWrapping="Wrap" MaxWidth="500" TextAlignment="Center">
                This usually means the WebView2 Runtime isn't installed on this computer. Download it from
                <Hyperlink NavigateUri="https://go.microsoft.com/fwlink/p/?LinkId=2124703"
                           RequestNavigate="DownloadLink_OnRequestNavigate">go.microsoft.com/fwlink/p/?LinkId=2124703</Hyperlink>
                (Evergreen WebView2 Runtime) and try again.
            </TextBlock>
            <TextBlock x:Name="FailureDetailTextBlock" Margin="0,10,0,0" Foreground="Gray"
                       TextWrapping="Wrap" MaxWidth="500" TextAlignment="Center" FontSize="11"/>
        </StackPanel>
    </Grid>
</Window>
